1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,927
In customer discovery, I heard: Finding a
bond’s CUSIP is such a pain.

2
00:00:07,927 --> 00:00:11,585
I don’t know where to buy.

3
00:00:11,585 --> 00:00:15,854
Fidelity’s bond account is not for me.

4
00:00:15,854 --> 00:00:20,732
I only want to invest a small amount.

5
00:00:20,732 --> 00:00:25,000
Different comments, one design challenge:
getting started.

6
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:32,636
How can someone with no bond experience
understand a few options and make their

7
00:00:32,636 --> 00:00:34,273
first small purchase?

8
00:00:34,273 --> 00:00:37,000
That’s the question behind InCreditble.

9
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:41,950
First, I tell the product I’m new to bonds.

10
00:00:41,950 --> 00:00:45,800
That changes how much explanation I get.

11
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:48,550
My risk preference is separate.

12
00:00:48,550 --> 00:00:55,700
Then I choose a yield target, a timeframe,
an industry and a budget.

13
00:00:55,700 --> 00:00:59,000
Let’s start with just twenty-five dollars.

14
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:04,250
I don’t need to start with a bond
identifier.

15
00:01:04,250 --> 00:01:09,500
The finder gives me three matches within my
preferences.

16
00:01:09,500 --> 00:01:17,083
I can compare an earlier repayment date, a
different industry and more interest,

17
00:01:17,083 --> 00:01:20,000
with the important trade-offs visible.

18
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:27,917
When I need help, I can ask about the
company or what could go wrong.

19
00:01:27,917 --> 00:01:34,250
Here, the assistant explains the risk of
missed payments and selling early.

20
00:01:34,250 --> 00:01:39,000
The explanations are optional; the decision
stays with me.

21
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:46,149
Now I see a sample price, with separate buy
and sell quotes.

22
00:01:46,149 --> 00:01:50,915
My twenty-five dollars buys part of a bond.

23
00:01:50,915 --> 00:01:59,851
Before confirming, I can see exactly what I
pay, the cash I’ll have left, expected

24
00:01:59,851 --> 00:02:02,830
interest and the repayment date.

25
00:02:02,830 --> 00:02:07,000
These are promised payments, not guaranteed
returns.

26
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:12,838
After I approve, the new holding appears and
my cash balance updates.

27
00:02:12,838 --> 00:02:17,703
The payment view helps me see when interest
is expected.

28
00:02:17,703 --> 00:02:24,027
Existing sample accounts stay visible
alongside this position, so I can see the

29
00:02:24,027 --> 00:02:25,000
wider picture.

30
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:30,634
Underneath, explicit filters and transparent
ranking narrow a pool of 672

31
00:02:30,634 --> 00:02:31,659
fictional bonds.

32
00:02:31,659 --> 00:02:36,780
The prototype tracks fractional positions,
settlement, cost basis and payment

33
00:02:36,780 --> 00:02:37,293
schedules.

34
00:02:37,293 --> 00:02:42,415
Assistant responses, identity checks, quotes
and connections are simulated; no

35
00:02:42,415 --> 00:02:46,000
live AI model or broker is connected.

36
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:52,545
Next, we’ll test whether first-time
investors can explain their purchase and its

37
00:02:52,545 --> 00:02:54,182
risks without coaching.

38
00:02:54,182 --> 00:02:54,727
InCreditble.

39
00:02:54,727 --> 00:02:56,364
Your first bond.

40
00:02:56,364 --> 00:02:58,000
At your pace.
